{# The document every page of the interaction plane is served in (architecture §5.2, §6): its language,
   which is the language of the interaction (§5.7), the theme it was asked for, the colours the tenant
   declared, the one stylesheet built from assets/styles/app.css, and the body a skeleton fills.

   Two skeletons extend this one, layout/interaction.html.twig and layout/account.html.twig, because the
   pages are of two kinds, and the layout the bundle hands them (templates/bundles/BeffroiBundle/) picks the
   one a route belongs to. What the two have in common is here and in no other file.

   The theme is on the document and not in a script (issue #447): light and dark are what the stylesheet
   declares, and a document that names neither leaves the answer to the browser.

   The colours the tenant declared (issue beffroi-auth/beffroi#449) are written in a style element of the
   head as the two custom properties DaisyUI draws a primary surface from: the accent of the buttons and
   the links, and the colour of what is written on them. They are in the document and not in the stylesheet
   because the stylesheet is built once for the deployment and these come from a row. The value is three or
   six hexadecimal digits, which is all the model lets a tenant say, so there is nothing else it could put
   there; a tenant that declared no colour leaves the element off and the themes answer.

   The element carries the nonce of the response and not a style attribute of the document, because a
   Content-Security-Policy names a nonce and cannot name an attribute: "style-src 'self'" refuses an inline
   attribute whatever is in it, and nothing but "unsafe-inline" would let one through
   (config/packages/nelmio_security.yaml). The nonce is drawn for this response alone, so the one block
   this page carries runs and an injected one does not. It comes after the stylesheet, which is what
   settles the two declarations against the ones a theme makes at the same specificity. #}
{% set chosen_theme = theme() %}
{% set tenant = beffroi_tenant() %}
{% set colored = tenant is not null and tenant.primaryColor is not null %}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html
    lang="{{ app.request.locale|replace({'_': '-'}) }}"
    {%- if chosen_theme.attribute() is not null %} data-theme="{{ chosen_theme.attribute() }}"{% endif %}
>
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>{% block title %}{% endblock %}</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('styles/app.css') }}">
    {% if colored %}
        <style nonce="{{ csp_nonce('style') }}">:root, html[data-theme] { --color-primary: {{ tenant.primaryColor }}; --color-primary-content: {{ tenant.primaryContentColor }}; }</style>
    {% endif %}
    {% block head %}{% endblock %}
</head>
<body class="min-h-dvh {% block surface %}bg-base-200{% endblock %}">
{% block body %}{% endblock %}
</body>
</html>
